Antigravity Implementation Plan — Speedometer Website UI & Product Improvements
Goal

Improve the existing Speedometer / Fast.com-style internet speed test website without breaking the current working speed-test engine.

Focus on:

Better UI/UX
Professional testing flow
Improved results presentation
Responsive design
Clean architecture
Production-ready frontend integration

Do not implement Google AdSense or advertising functionality in this phase.

Phase 1 — Analyze Existing Project

Before changing code:

Inspect the current project structure.
Identify:
Speed test engine
API calls
Railway backend integration
LibreSpeed integration
Current gauge/speedometer component
State management
Existing animations
Preserve all currently working measurement logic.
Identify duplicated or unnecessary frontend logic.
Fix existing UI-related errors without changing measurement behavior.
Rule

Do not rewrite the speed test engine unless required for integration.

Phase 2 — Create Clean Application Architecture

Separate the frontend into logical modules.

src/
├── app/
│   ├── page
│   ├── layout
│   └── globals
│
├── components/
│   ├── layout/
│   │   ├── Header
│   │   └── Footer
│   │
│   ├── speedtest/
│   │   ├── SpeedTest
│   │   ├── Speedometer
│   │   ├── TestProgress
│   │   ├── TestStatus
│   │   ├── MetricCard
│   │   └── TestResults
│   │
│   └── ui/
│
├── hooks/
│   └── speed-test
│
├── services/
│   └── speed-test
│
├── types/
│   └── speed-test
│
└── lib/

Adapt this structure to the existing project instead of blindly moving working code.

Phase 3 — Improve Test State Management

Create a clear test lifecycle.

IDLE
  ↓
CONNECTING
  ↓
SELECTING_SERVER
  ↓
TESTING_LATENCY
  ↓
TESTING_DOWNLOAD
  ↓
TESTING_UPLOAD
  ↓
COMPLETED

Also support:

ERROR
CANCELLED
Requirements

The UI must react to the actual test state.

Examples:

Don't show upload results before upload testing begins.
Don't show completed results while the test is running.
Show meaningful status text.
Prevent multiple tests from running simultaneously.
Allow restarting after completion.
