UI priorities
Current speed value
Current test phase
Speedometer animation
Progress information
Technical details
Phase 5 — Improve Speedometer Behavior

The gauge must use real measurement values.

Requirements
No fake speed animation.
Needle/value follows actual measured speed.
Smooth interpolation between incoming measurements.
Avoid visual jumping.
Support Mbps and Gbps.
Reset correctly before a new test.
Stop animation when testing finishes.
Important

The UI animation must not modify the actual measurement data.

Measurement Engine
        ↓
Real Speed Data
        ↓
UI State
        ↓
Smooth Visual Animation

The visual layer is separate from the measurement layer.

Phase 6 — Add Professional Test Progress

Show the current testing sequence visually.

● Connection
● Server
● Ping
◉ Download
○ Upload
○ Complete
Behavior

Completed stages:

✓

Current stage:

Active animation

Upcoming stages:

Inactive

The progress component must be driven by real test state.

Phase 7 — Improve Live Metrics

During testing, show live metrics.

DOWNLOAD
245.67 Mbps

UPLOAD
Testing...

PING
12 ms
Rules
Download updates during download testing.
Upload updates during upload testing.
Ping remains visible once measured.
Don't display incorrect placeholder values.
Clearly indicate metrics that are still being tested.
Phase 8 — Build a Better Results Experience

After completion, transition to a results view.

YOUR INTERNET SPEED

┌────────────────┐
│ DOWNLOAD       │
│ 245.67 Mbps    │
└────────────────┘

┌────────────────┐
│ UPLOAD         │
│ 48.21 Mbps     │
└────────────────┘

┌────────────────┐
│ PING           │
│ 12 ms          │
└────────────────┘

┌────────────────┐
│ JITTER         │
│ 3 ms           │
└────────────────┘

Include:

Download speed
Upload speed
Ping
Jitter, if available from the engine
Server information
Test completion time

Actions:

[ TEST AGAIN ]

Do not add sharing functionality unless the existing architecture supports it cleanly.

Phase 9 — Improve Error Handling UI

Create user-friendly states for:

Server unavailable
Connection failure
CORS/network failure
Test timeout
Backend unavailable
Unexpected measurement failure

Example:

Unable to complete the speed test.

The test server could not be reached.

[ TRY AGAIN ]
Requirements
Never expose raw backend errors directly to users.
Log technical errors safely for debugging.
Keep error UI consistent with the main design.
Phase 10 — Improve Header and Navigation

Create a minimal modern header.

Desktop
LOGO

Speed Test
How It Works
About

Theme Toggle
Mobile
LOGO              MENU

Requirements:

Sticky only if it improves the existing design.
No heavy navigation animations.
Smooth mobile menu.
Active navigation states.

Do not overload the header.

Phase 11 — Improve Visual System

Standardize the design system.

Define consistent:

Typography
Display text
Heading
Body
Small labels
Metric values
Spacing

Use a consistent spacing scale.

Components

Standardize:

Buttons
Cards
Status indicators
Progress elements
Metric displays
Visual style

Maintain:

Dark interface
Glassmorphism where appropriate
Subtle gradients
Controlled glow effects
Important

Reduce unnecessary:

Excessive blur
Constant glowing
Heavy animations
Visual noise

The speed result must remain the visual focus.

Phase 12 — Responsive Implementation

Test these breakpoints:

Mobile
Tablet
Desktop
Large Desktop
Mobile requirements
Speedometer scales correctly.
Metrics stack vertically.
Large touch targets.
No horizontal overflow.
Text remains readable.
Animation performance remains smooth.
Desktop requirements
Better use of horizontal space.
Results can use grid layout.
Speedometer remains centered.
Supporting information stays secondary.
Phase 13 — Animation Improvements

Use animation only to communicate state.

Implement transitions for:

Test start
Stage changes
Speed value updates
Result completion
Error appearance

Avoid:

Infinite decorative animations.
Heavy background effects.
Animations that reduce speed-test performance.

Respect reduced-motion preferences where possible.

Phase 14 — Performance Optimization

Optimize the frontend because the website itself must remain fast.

Check:

Unnecessary re-renders.
Excessive state updates.
Animation frame performance.
Heavy dependencies.
Unoptimized SVGs.
Large assets.
Memory leaks during repeated tests.
Important

The speedometer UI must not consume significant resources during testing because it could affect the user's measured network/device performance.

Phase 15 — Integration Rules

The frontend must integrate with the existing Railway/LibreSpeed backend.

Requirements:

Use the configured backend base URL.
Centralize API configuration.
Do not hardcode localhost URLs in production code.
Handle development and production environments separately.
Preserve existing CORS-compatible endpoints.
Do not duplicate speed-test requests.
Ensure only one active measurement session at a time.
Phase 16 — Validation and Testing

Test the complete lifecycle:

Initial Load
    ↓
Start Test
    ↓
Connect
    ↓
Server Selection
    ↓
Ping
    ↓
Download
    ↓
Upload
    ↓
Results
    ↓
Test Again

Also test:

Slow connections.
Backend failures.
Mobile devices.
Repeated tests.
Page refresh during test.
Network interruption.
Railway deployment.
Phase 17 — Final Code Quality Pass

Before completing:

Check
No unused components.
No duplicated logic.
No fake metrics.
No hardcoded production URLs.
No exposed secrets.
No unnecessary API calls.
No console errors.
No broken TypeScript types.
No hydration errors.
No mobile overflow.
No UI regression.
